  "decision": {
    "answer": "SUPPORTS",
    "explanation": "The provided evidence from pmid-27283860 describes a phase 2 trial evaluating the combination of dabrafenib and trametinib in patients with previously treated metastatic BRAF V600E-mutant non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC). The study reports an investigator-assessed confirmed overall response rate of 63.2%, including complete and partial responses. This directly supports the claim that the combination of dabrafenib and trametinib is associated with sensitivity/response in NSCLC patients with somatic BRAF V600E mutations.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "document_id": "pmid-27283860",
        "start": 0,
        "end": 476,
        "quote": "In this phase 2, multicenter, nonrandomized, open-label study of patients with pretreated metastatic BRAF V600E-mutant NSCLC, antitumor activity and safety of oral dabrafenib (150 mg twice daily) plus oral trametinib (2 mg once daily) were evaluated. . . . With a median follow-up of 11.6 months (IQR 8.8-15.2), the investigator-assessed confirmed overall response was 63.2% (36 of 57; 95% CI 49.3-75.6), including 2 (3.5%) of 57 patients with CR and 34 (59.6%) of 57 with PR."
      }
    ],
